  "body": "Independent native FP16 AWQ GEMM source checkpoint: complete first wave64/block visit and first barrier resumption, followed by the guarded per-lane A-staging phase. All 31/47 setup instructions and both complete eight-iteration A loops are proved against the full 138/226-instruction source template, including exact shared values, input preservation, outside-memory frames and source-ordered trace effects.\n\nThe standalone archive contains 20 owned Lean modules and four complete source instances. Fresh builds and an independent replay without Git or an owned compiled cache reproduce 208 library plus 48 source audits (256 total), using only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. Six changed sources are rejected logically; 21 fully rehashed stage claims are rejected before extraction. The reader also replays the earlier 90-audit checkpoint. All new modules retain maxRecDepth=10000 and maxHeartbeats=2000000; machine fuel, shape bounds and kernel source are unchanged.\n\nThis is a partial execution checkpoint with zero AWQ source certificates. B staging, matrix/K-loop execution, output stores, whole-trace race freedom and dense-reference equality remain unfinished. The earlier release native-awq-gemm-checkpoint-20261112 retains paired MI350 numerical evidence: 120 launches, 820,224 CPU float64 comparisons, zero tolerance failures and zero cross-host output bit differences. This proof checkpoint adds no GPU launches or model calls. Original paper model/token/NVIDIA results are not asserted.\n"
